{"repositoryId":1152379049,"availability":"available","full":"flooooooooooow/flow","name":"flow","description":"A statically typed language for systems that evolve through time. Algebraic effects, autodiff, C and MLIR backends.","category":"Design","language":"C","stars":5,"forks":1,"created":"2026-02-07T19:38:00Z","updated":"2026-10-19T00:21:09Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://flooooooooooow.github.io/flow/","topics":["algebraic-effects","automatic-differentiation","c-backend","compiler","language-design","mlir","programming-language","realtime","systems-programming"],"demo":"https://flooooooooooow.github.io/flow/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T00:41:15.798Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T00:41:15.798Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T00:41:15.798Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T19:08:20.723Z","stars":5,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-19T00:41:15.798Z","stars":5,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A language for systems that evolve through time","Flow is a statically typed, compiled systems language built around one idea: you describe how a system evolves through time, and that description is the program. The production path is the self-hosted flowc compiler with a portable C backend. Algebraic effects, dynamics and control DSLs, verification, advanced stdlib domains, and alternate backends ship as explicitly Experimental surfaces until they are promoted.","The compatibility promise is defined in STABILITY.md. Linux x86-64 and macOS arm64 are the Tier-1 platforms; every published release is qualified from the exact tag before GitHub Release publication."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/flooooooooooow/flow/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b7e9094bb351290cb04bcb46fa5f35222a80785622ea6bf85a41166ac01c69e4","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:20.843Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:20.843Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A language for sy